  "note": "Total Assets = Total Liabilities + Equity reconciles exactly. This is the first year (unlike 2011-2012) where Note 7.3 splits the Mumbai branch's own loans into classified/unclassified rather than treating the whole branch as unclassified — classified_loans_total (4,437,909,516) is the true grand total (in-Bangladesh 4,355,300,407 + Mumbai 82,609,109), but the substandard/doubtful/bad_loss sub-categories above are in-Bangladesh only (Mumbai's 82,609,109 classified balance is not broken into sub-categories in the source), so those three sub-category values sum to 4,355,300,407, not to classified_loans_total. Source PDF -layout extraction shows the same stray-leading-artifact-number pattern seen in other years (e.g. two extra numbers glued before the Substandard/Doubtful rows); resolved via the same arithmetic-reconciliation method used throughout this dataset (the correct column reconciles exactly against the printed subtotal, the artifact does not). The bank's own 2014 Q1 report restates this quarter's EPS comparative to 0.30 (vs 0.34 contemporaneous here) — a bonus-share weighted-average-share restatement (paid-up capital rose from 4,423,336,680 at this date to 4,976,253,760 by Q1 2014). Contemporaneous value (0.34) is kept per project convention."
